# VTID-03723 — commands actually run.

# --- Why this exists -------------------------------------------------------
#
# Reported live, repeatedly, on staging: Polish and Portuguese sessions spoke
# the correct-accent voice but the WORDS were English. Every prior fix in
# this chain (VTID-03711 PCM rate, VTID-03720 cascade flag, VTID-03721 cascade
# health endpoint, VTID-03722 cascade turn boundary) was real and individually
# verified — and none of it moved the symptom, because none of those code
# paths were ever reached.

# --- Root cause, confirmed live against staging -----------------------------

curl -s "https://preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/orb/health"
#   -> {"model":"gemini-2.0-flash-exp","transport":"SSE","gemini_configured":true,...}
#   Decisive: a live session is instantiating the Gemini/Vertex client, not
#   Nova and not the cascade — despite Vertex being permanently dead since
#   the GCP shutdown (2026-08-16).

curl -s "https://preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/orb/active-provider"
#   -> {"active_provider":"vertex","effectiveProvider":"vertex","reason":"default_vertex",...}
#   staging's voice.active_provider system_config row is 'vertex'.

# Cross-checked: has the cascade EVER fired, on any session, ever?
#   SELECT count(*) FROM oasis_events WHERE type LIKE 'orb.upstream.cascaded.%'
#   -> 0 (read-only query against production, prior session)
#   Zero successes AND zero failures — not "rarely used", structurally
#   unreachable, because selectUpstreamProvider() returned {provider:'vertex'}
#   before the cascade (or Nova) was ever consulted.

# --- Source-level confirmation: count the vertex return sites ---------------

grep -c "provider: 'vertex'" \
  services/gateway/src/orb/live/upstream/upstream-provider-selector.ts
#   -> 11 (before this fix)

grep -c "provider: 'vertex'" \
  services/gateway/src/orb/live/upstream/upstream-provider-selector.ts
#   -> 0 (after this fix — see the diff)

# Two more hardcoded sites found OUTSIDE the selector that would have
# defeated the fix even with the selector corrected:
grep -n "provider: 'vertex'" services/gateway/src/routes/orb-live.ts
#   -> (before) L7137 config-read-failure catch-block default
#   -> (before) L7157 idle-Nova-rotation-exhaustion override
#   -> (after)  0 matches for an unconditional provider:'vertex' assignment
#      (the remaining 'vertex' occurrences are diagnostic labels in gated
#      Nova-retry branches, corrected to 'nova_sonic' to match reality)

